{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he begot in his likeness, after his image.</b> It is well known that all creatures born of the living are in the likeness and image of those who beget them. But because man was exalted in his likeness and image — as it says of him (Genesis 5:1), \"in the likeness of Elohim He made him\" — Scripture explains here that his offspring too were in that exalted likeness. It did not say this concerning Cain and Abel, because it did not wish to elaborate upon them, but it did explain it concerning Seth, because the world was established from him, or else because man was created in the perfection of formation, it declared concerning Seth that he was like him in strength and in beauty."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:20:51.740905374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}